# DiMovie — Environment Variables

## apps/api (.env)

```env
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=4000
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5433/dimovie
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
JWT_ACCESS_SECRET=change-me-access-min-32-chars-long!!
JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=change-me-refresh-min-32-chars-long!
JWT_ACCESS_TTL=15m
JWT_REFRESH_TTL=30d
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000
# Leave empty when web proxies via /backend (same-site cookies)
COOKIE_DOMAIN=
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
R2_BUCKET=dimovie-uploads
R2_PUBLIC_URL=
MEDIASOUP_LISTEN_IP=0.0.0.0
MEDIASOUP_ANNOUNCED_IP=127.0.0.1
TURN_URLS=turn:localhost:3478
TURN_USERNAME=dimovie
TURN_CREDENTIAL=dimovie
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL=http://localhost:4000/auth/google/callback
DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=
DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET=
DISCORD_CALLBACK_URL=http://localhost:4000/auth/discord/callback
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
STRIPE_PRO_PRICE_ID=
STRIPE_ENTERPRISE_PRICE_ID=
```

## apps/web (.env.local)

```env
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_NAME=DiMovie
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4000
NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4000
```

## Railway (api service)

1. Add PostgreSQL + Redis plugins; wire `DATABASE_URL` and `REDIS_URL`.
2. Set all `apps/api` secrets above (strong JWT secrets, production `CORS_ORIGIN`).
3. Set `CORS_ORIGIN` / `FRONTEND_URL` to the Vercel URL (e.g. `https://dimovie.vercel.app`).
4. Leave `COOKIE_DOMAIN` empty if the web app proxies API via `/backend`.
5. `MEDIASOUP_ANNOUNCED_IP` — public IP if using SFU; voice falls back to P2P if mediasoup fails.
6. Deploy uses `apps/api/Dockerfile`; entrypoint runs `prisma migrate deploy` then starts the API.
7. Healthcheck: `GET /health`.

## Vercel (web)

Root directory: `apps/web` (vercel.json already sets monorepo install/build).

```env
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_NAME=DiMovie
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://YOUR-API.up.railway.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL=https://YOUR-API.up.railway.app
```

Browser HTTP goes through `/backend` rewrite; WebSocket/OAuth use `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` directly.
